      "resolution": {
        "action": "adapt",
        "commit": "4232283925521b3f5428491e89417b9972c464dd",
        "automatic": false,
        "rationale": "10feeb0 is the workflow-retention commit of an earlier sync review that alas still carries and the sync replays as a non-ledger fork commit. Its only hunk pins amannn/action-semantic-pull-request in conventional-prs.yml to 48f2562 (v6.1.1) over the line it found then (2252a14, v6.1.2); upstream v2.12.1 (#807) changes that same line to c5e23b7 (v6.1.3), so the pick conflicted. The adaptation 4232283 (stacked on the exact candidate at its replay point) keeps 10feeb0's result: the same single path and the same added line; only the replaced line is now upstream's v6.1.3 pin. The candidate's .github/workflows tree is restored to alas's as for any upstream workflow change, and the integration's .github tree equals alas.",
        "tests": [
          "scripts/sync-review.test.mjs",
          "scripts/sync-reviewed-exceptions.test.mjs",
          "scripts/sync-downstream-transitions.test.mjs"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "upstreamWorkflowChanges": [
    {
      "path": ".github/workflows/conventional-prs.yml",
      "resolution": {
        "action": "retain-downstream",
        "automatic": false,
        "rationale": "Upstream v2.12.1 (#807, Dependabot) only bumps the pinned amannn/action-semantic-pull-request in conventional-prs.yml from 2252a14 (v6.1.2) to c5e23b7 (v6.1.3). alas still pins 2252a14, and the publication verifier requires the candidate's .github/workflows tree to equal the previous alas tree, so the candidate keeps alas's workflow unchanged. The workflow only validates pull request titles against main and never runs on alas; the pin bump can be mirrored in a separate level-3 automation/* PR after this sync. It changes no step, input or permission.",
        "tests": [
          "scripts/sync-review.test.mjs",
          "scripts/sync-reviewed-exceptions.test.mjs"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
